Several things.

NetHack is too easy for experienced players, which is why a lot of them
have floated away to Crawl, but at the same time unforgiving of new
players.

The difficulty is rather uneven. The opening game is hard, which
contributes to the unforgivingness, but if you get over that hump there's
then a long very easy section in the middle game broken up by occasional
known problems (Medusa, some Nemeses). Then the endgame is a bit harder
but of widely varying difficulty. See Demogorgon? A summoning storm on
Air? Your endgame just got much harder.

The other main gripe is that there are a number of techniques which are
easily repeatable, pose no serious challenge, and improve your position.
Alchemy springs to mind. Once you've acquired the basic habit of potion
discipline, here's an extra 250 max HP for you if you know about alchemy!
